    "result_text": "The build is green. All changes are complete and the test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `telephoneDisplay` field, which returns the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\nThree changes, following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring PetClinic REST app:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived fields like `displayName`/`contactPreference`). The DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Added `toDisplay(String e164)` (and a small `countryCodeOf` helper), reusing the same country codes the normalizer already recognises (`+61` AU, `+1` NANP). It splits the `+`/country-code prefix, inserts a space, and groups the national digits in threes. `null` in \u2192 `null` out; an unrecognised/non-E.164 value is returned unchanged.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired `telephoneDisplay` into `toOwnerDto` via a `toTelephoneDisplay(owner)` default method that delegates to the normalizer \u2014 matching how `ageBand`, `displayName`, etc. are mapped.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` confirms `0412 345 678` \u2192 stored `telephone` `+61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay` `+61 412 345 678`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nNote: this repo isn't a git repository, so I made no commit \u2014 let me know if you'd like me to initialize one.",
