        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `toDisplay` lives in `TelephoneNormalizer`, which the class Javadoc already declares the single source of truth for telephone handling. It reuses the existing `DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE`/`NANP_COUNTRY_CODE` constants rather than introducing new ones, and the new private `countryCodeOf` helper mirrors the existing `hasValidNationalLength`/`nationalLength` helper structure.\n- **The mapper delegate matches its siblings exactly.** `toTelephoneDisplay(Owner)` is a thin `default` delegate wired via `@Mapping(expression=...)`, identical in shape to `toContactPreference`, `toAgeBand`, `toLocality`, etc., and it delegates to the normalizer just as `normalizeTelephone` does \u2014 no formatting logic leaks into the mapper.\n- **No new catch-all.** Nothing is piling into the wrong class; the OpenAPI `telephoneDisplay` entry follows the existing read-only-field convention.\n\nMinor (non-blocking) observation: `countryCodeOf` and `hasValidNationalLength` now both enumerate the same two country codes via `startsWith`, so a future maintainer could express `hasValidNationalLength` in terms of `countryCodeOf` to centralize country-code recognition. That's an optional tidy-up of pre-existing code, not a defect in this additive change."
      }
